KEYBINDINGS SURVEY

This folder holds Tamlinux's survey of keybinding systems across other
operating systems, actively maintained Linux and UNIX distributions, and
influential programs. Keybindings are a fundamental design pillar of
Tamlinux: tam-pane (compositor), tam-last (terminal), tam-clam (shell),
tam (guide), and sibling tools (tam-edit, tam-file, tam-view) should
share one ergonomic, mnemonic, internally logical system across both
text and graphical surfaces.

Start with synthesis.md. Each topic file follows the README-ideas format
(What it is, Modifier semantics and chord grammar, Ideas worth taking
with verdicts, Things to avoid, Where to look) and notes that it is a
reference survey of documented designs to inform ../arch/keybindings.md.


